  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WAN-IFRA Strenghtening independent media programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WAN-IFRA&apos;s mission is to protect the rights of journalists across the world to operate free media and provide its members with professional services to help their business prosper in a digital world and perform their crucial role in open societies. Specific trainings include applying techniques to combat sexual harassment in the work place, and in ensuring gender equality in the media sector. 
The Project will focus on three priority themes: safety of journalists, media plurality and diverse opinions and perspectives.The immediate target groups are editors, journalists and senior professionals in selected media partner organisations in Vietnam, Myanmar, The Philippines, Indonesia, Kenya, Uganda and Tanzania.</narrative>
  </description>
